    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Generate a Detailed User Story based on the FRD\n{{ $json.output }}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a Senior Business Analyst with expertise in Warehouse Management Systems (WMS), OMS, Marketplace and E-commerce domains.\n\nConvert the provided requirement into a User Story using EXACTLY the format below.\n\nOutput Format:\n\nRequirement Title\n\n<Generated Requirement Title>\n\nUser Story\n\nAs a <Role>\nI want <Functionality>\nSo that <Business Benefit>\n\nAcceptance Criteria\n\nScenario 1: <Scenario Name>\n\nGiven <Precondition>\nWhen <Action>\nThen <Expected Result>\n\nScenario 2: <Scenario Name>\n\nGiven <Precondition>\nWhen <Action>\nThen <Expected Result>\n\nScenario 3: <Scenario Name>\n\nGiven <Precondition>\nWhen <Action>\nThen <Expected Result>\n\nGenerate all relevant positive, negative and validation scenarios.\n\nBusiness Rules\n\n* Rule 1\n* Rule 2\n* Rule 3\n\nAdditional Instructions:\n\n1. Generate a minimum of 3 Acceptance Criteria scenarios.\n2. Include both positive and negative scenarios whenever applicable.\n3. Include validation rules as acceptance criteria.\n4. Use business-friendly language.\n5. Do not generate Epics.\n6. Do not generate Assumptions.\n7. Do not generate Dependencies.\n8. Do not generate Test Cases separately.\n9. Do not use markdown symbols such as ###, **, or JSON.\n10. Return only the final user story document.\n11. Consider real-world WMS, OMS and Marketplace validations.\n"
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        352,
        -48
      ],
      "id": "5ebeed07-fd6b-4c50-92ae-b7f8830e5067",
      "name": "User Story Generator"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Review the following User Story and Improve it ,if needed\n{{$json.output}}",
        "options": {
          "systemMessage": "You are a Senior Product Owner and Business Analyst.\n\nReview the provided user story.\n\nValidate the following:\n\n1. User story follows Agile standards.\n2. Acceptance Criteria are complete.\n3. Positive scenarios are covered.\n4. Negative scenarios are covered.\n5. Validation scenarios are covered.\n6. Business Rules are complete.\n7. Missing edge cases are identified.\n8. User roles are correctly defined.\n9. Audit requirements are included where applicable.\n10. Inventory, Order, Shipment and Marketplace impacts are considered where relevant.\n\nIf information is missing, improve the user story.\n\nReturn the FINAL improved user story only.\n\nDo not explain what was changed.\n\nDo not provide comments.\n\nReturn the complete revised document.\n"
        }
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.agent",
      "typeVersion": 3.1,
      "position": [
        704,
        -48
      ],
      "id": "97b33ba7-af07-4944-bba2-4c0d105256ce",
      "name": "User Story Reviewer"
    },
